This package is a Swift/MLX port of HEART — Hybrid Efficient Attention with Rank-factorized bias
Transformer — by Philip Hofmann (Phips), https://huggingface.co/Phips/HEART, Apache-2.0
(code and pretrained weights; revision 868878ce4c253a8061300f923b620fdc6edf090a). The released
checkpoints re-hosted at mlx-community/HEART-fp16 and mlx-community/HEART-fp32 are per-tensor
exact conversions of the upstream files (see oracle/convert_weights.py); they were trained by the
author only on Phips/lucid-cc0-v2-hc-512 (CC0).

The port's Sources/HEARTMLX/HEART.swift is an isomorphic derivative of:
  • heart_arch.py — Philip Hofmann, Apache-2.0 (Phips/HEART);
  • traiNNer-redux traiNNer/archs/hat_iln_arch.py and the iLN class of traiNNer/archs/arch_util.py —
    the-database and contributors, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/the-database/traiNNer-redux
    (revision 686293190aca3e432a42b6155dbc94ea51c4bf9f);
which in turn build on:
  • HAT — Chen et al., "Activating More Pixels in Image Super-Resolution Transformer", XPixelGroup,
    Apache-2.0, https://github.com/XPixelGroup/HAT (arXiv 2205.04437);
  • HAT-iLN — the i-LN normalisation (arXiv 2504.06629);
  • SST's RIB — Rank-factorized Implicit Neural Bias for window attention (arXiv 2603.06738).

Tiling infrastructure (MLXTileProcessor, PlaybackTier) is consumed from xocialize/mlx-realesrgan-swift
(Apache-2.0). MLX and MLX-Swift are © Apple Inc., MIT.
